<title>USA: Evans to sell non-income producing assets.</title>
<headline>Evans to sell non-income producing assets.</headline>
<dateline>BAY CITY, Texas 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Evans Systems Inc said at its annual meeting on March 28 it has identified approximately $3.1 million of non-income producing assets to be put up for sale with the proceeds to be used to expand its ChemWay and Convenience Store divisions.</p>
<p>The company also said the shareholders reelected J. L. Evans, Sr., David Deerman and Carl Schafer to three year terms on the Board of Directors and adopted the authorization of 1.5 million preferred shares.</p>
<p>ChemWay produces and markets automotive chemical products. Convenience Stores is a chain of 40 retail outlets in South Texas and Louisiana. Evans' other units are Petroleum Marketing and EDCO Environmental Systems.</p>
</text>
